      <h2>Why Run AI Agents on a VPS?</h2>
      <p>Cloud AI services like OpenAI's GPT-4o or Anthropic's Claude are powerful but get expensive at scale. A single AI agent making 1,000 API calls per day can cost $50-200/month depending on model choice. Self-hosted models on a VPS reduce per-call costs to near zero after the initial server investment.</p>
      <p>The trade-off? You need to manage your own infrastructure. But for developers running multiple agents, automation workflows, or prototype products, the economics are compelling.</p>

      <h2>VPS Recommendations for AI Agents</h2>
      <p>Not every VPS is suitable for AI agent workloads. Here's what matters:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>RAM</strong>: Minimum 4GB for lightweight models (Llama 3.1 8B). For 70B models, 32GB+ required.</li>
        <li><strong>Storage</strong>: NVMe strongly preferred — model loading is I/O heavy.</li>
        <li><strong>Bandwidth</strong>: API calls to external providers need reliable network.</li>
        <li><strong>CPU</strong>: AMD EPYC or Intel Xeon for good inference performance.</li>
      </ul>

